[ system ]
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set zerochance = ss.silenceChancePercent %}
{% set tagCompanion = ss.tagCompanion %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}
{# playerIsLastTarget: the last line was aimed at the player, so the player is owed the next turn. #}
{% set playerIsLastTarget = existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "UUID") and lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}
{# zeroAvailable: a single flag that governs EVERY mention of `0` in this prompt.
   `0` is on the ballot if the normal silence roll allows it OR the player was just addressed. #}
{% set zeroAvailable = (random < zerochance) or playerIsLastTarget %}
{# PLACEHOLDER — these two fields do not exist in get_speaker_selector_settings() yet.
   followerInterruption is one of: "stay_out" "rare" "sometimes" "often" "jump_in"
   nonFollowerInterruption is one of: "stay_out" "low" "medium" "chatty"
   The exact encoding (string vs int) is not final; wire it to the real setting when the plugin exposes it. #}
{% set followerInterruption = ss.followerInterruption %}
{% set nonFollowerInterruption = ss.nonFollowerInterruption %}
# Task
One line was just spoken. Decide who, if anyone, speaks in the very next beat. Output only {% if zeroAvailable %}`0` or {% endif %}`[speaker]>[target]`

## Output Format
{% if zeroAvailable %}- `0` = no NPC speaks this beat (the moment turns to the player or to no one)
{% endif %}- `Lydia>player` = Lydia speaks to player
- `Ulfric Stormcloak>Galmar Stone-Fist` = Ulfric speaks to Galmar

## How to choose the speaker
This is ONE judgment, not a checklist run on each candidate. Read the conversation as it stands right now and ask a single question: given exactly what was just said, which one person in the room does this moment turn the floor toward{% if zeroAvailable %}, or does it turn toward no present NPC{% endif %}?

Compare, on equal footing:
- the person the last line was aimed at{% if existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") and not playerIsLastTarget %} ({{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}){% endif %},
- every other candidate listed below,{% if zeroAvailable %}
- and the option that no NPC speaks (`0`).{% endif %}

Pick the single one that a listener who knew all of these characters would most expect to speak next. Not "who could plausibly say something" — run that test and almost everyone passes, because most characters always could. Ask instead "who does THIS line call on."

A line calls on someone when:
- It is aimed at them, asks them something, or names them.
- It touches something that is specifically theirs as written in their profile or Interjection guidance — their duty in this exact situation, an allegiance or conviction the line directly challenges, a person they care about, an expertise the line invites — strongly enough that a reader would look to them in particular, not merely grant that they have an opinion.
{% if tagCompanion %}- They are the player's companion AND the last line is the kind of thing this specific companion, as written, reacts to. Not "a companion, so they talk" — this one, because of who they are and what was just said.
{% endif %}
A line does NOT call on someone merely because they are present, nearby, listed, a companion in the abstract, a guard or merchant in the abstract, or capable of holding an opinion on the topic.

If two or more people are genuinely called on, choose the one the last line lands on most directly. {% if zeroAvailable %}If no one is — the line was aimed at the player, closed the exchange, or engages no one here in particular — output `0`.{% else %}Someone speaks this beat, so choose the person the moment turns toward most, even if faintly; do not invent a reaction the line does not support.{% endif %}

## Whether `0` is available this beat
{% if zeroAvailable %}`0` is a full option in the comparison above — it is not a gate you check first, and not a preference. It simply means the moment turns to the player or to no present NPC.
{% if playerIsLastTarget %}The last line was aimed at the player, so `0` is available regardless of the silence roll: the player is owed the chance to answer. A companion or bystander may still be selected if the last line genuinely calls on them harder than it calls for the player's reply — but the default expectation here is that the player answers, i.e. `0`.
{% endif %}{% else %}`0` is NOT available this beat. Someone must speak. Choose the single person the moment most turns toward.
{% endif %}
## Interruption preference (a dial on the comparison, not a separate step)
"Already in the exchange" means the person the last line was aimed at (the natural responder) and, when the player was just addressed, the player. Everyone else is entering a conversation they were not part of. The two settings below only adjust how hard the last line must call on such an entering person before they win the comparison over the natural responder{% if zeroAvailable %} or over `0`{% endif %}. They never add a speaker the comparison would not already weigh, and never remove a candidate row. At the most permissive positions they add no restriction at all and selection is the pure comparison above.
{% if tagCompanion %}
**Follower entering the exchange** — for a candidate who is the player's follower and was not the one just addressed:
{% if followerInterruption == "stay_out" %}Do not select such a follower this beat. Their row stays; they may win a later beat. A follower who WAS the person just addressed is unaffected.
{% elif followerInterruption == "rare" %}They win only when the last line is aimed at them, names them, or their duty to the player squarely requires it.
{% elif followerInterruption == "sometimes" %}As "rare", and also when the last line squarely engages their Interjection guidance or a person, allegiance, or family named in their profile.
{% elif followerInterruption == "often" %}As "sometimes", and also when the last line is the kind of thing this particular follower, by their written personality, would react to — even unnamed.
{% elif followerInterruption == "jump_in" %}No extra bar. The follower competes on equal footing with the person just addressed; judge purely by the comparison above.
{% endif %}{% endif %}
**Non-follower entering the exchange** — for a candidate who is not a follower and was not the one just addressed:
{% if nonFollowerInterruption == "stay_out" %}Do not select such a non-follower this beat. Their row stays; they may win a later beat. A non-follower who WAS the person just addressed is unaffected.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == "low" %}They win only when the last line is aimed at them, names them, or their role squarely requires a response here.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == "medium" %}As "low", and also when the last line squarely engages their Interjection guidance or a person named in their profile.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == "chatty" %}As "medium", and also when the last line intersects their written personality or interests strongly enough to pull them in — even unnamed. Mere presence and the player's delay are still not reasons.
{% endif %}
**Restrictions:**
- Never select a {% if tagCompanion %}non-companion {% endif %}NPC just because they're listed — proximity alone is not a reason for bystanders to speak.
- Honor each NPC's Interjection guidance strictly.
- Do NOT select {{ lastSpeaker.name }} as speaker (they just spoke — but they CAN be selected as target).
{% if existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}- {{ lastSpeaker.name }} was addressing {% if playerIsLastTarget %}the player{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}{% endif %}. {% if playerIsLastTarget %}The player is the natural next speaker; select an NPC only if the last line calls on them harder than it calls for the player's answer.{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }} is the most likely next speaker if the exchange warrants a reply, but is not the only possible one.{% endif %}
{% endif %}- **No meta-commentary about silence** — never select an NPC to comment on the player not talking, to urge the player to speak, to urge an action out of impatience, or to narrate the waiting. NPCs simply wait.
- Regular NPCs cannot hear Virtual NPCs. {% if tagCompanion %}Companions *may* hear Virtual NPCs, if they are with the player and selected as a target of Virtual NPC dialogue. {% endif %}Do not select an NPC to respond directly to a Virtual NPC{% if tagCompanion %} unless they are a companion and they are responding to Virtual NPC dialogue they heard{% endif %}.
- Virtual NPCs may be selected as speaker but may NOT be selected as a target unless the speaker is also a Virtual NPC {% if tagCompanion %}or a companion{% endif %}.

{{ get_scene_context(0, 0, "full")}}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
## Location
{{ location }}

## Recent Dialogue
{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}

